1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:02,063
(Penny(arriving with a man in tow):)I'm hoping.

2
00:00:02,230 --> 00:00:03,270
(Sheldon:)Renaissance fair?

3
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:05,690
More of a medieval-slash-
Age of Enlightenment...

4
00:00:05,859 --> 00:00:09,069
(Sheldon:)...slash-
any-excuse-to-wear-a-codpiece fair.

5
00:00:09,488 --> 00:00:12,238
(Penny:)Okay, fine, whatever.
Um, you guys, this is my friend Eric.

6
00:00:12,407 --> 00:00:14,537
- Hello.
ERIC: Hey.

7
00:00:17,621 --> 00:00:19,951
(Leonard:)So, yeah, good to see you.

8
00:00:20,624 --> 00:00:22,664
(Penny:)Yeah. Yeah, it's good to see you too.

9
00:00:24,086 --> 00:00:25,716
- We should probably go.
- Yeah.

10
00:00:25,879 --> 00:00:29,129
- Bye, guys.
- Like your hat.

11
00:00:30,258 --> 00:00:32,678
(Howard:)Thanks, my mom made it.

12
00:00:34,679 --> 00:00:38,019
Penny with a new guy. Très awkward.

13
00:00:38,725 --> 00:00:41,185
(Leonard:)It wasn't awkward.

14
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:45,190
(Leonard:)It wasn't fun.
Besides, what's the big deal?

15
00:00:45,357 --> 00:00:48,777
(Leonard:)We dated, we stopped dating,
and now we're both moving on.

16
00:00:48,944 --> 00:00:51,614
By "moving on," you mean
she's going out with other men...

17
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:55,910
...and you spend the afternoon
making 15th-century soap with Wolowitz?

18
00:00:56,368 --> 00:00:58,038
That was not 15th-century soap.

19
00:00:58,203 --> 00:01:01,243
(Sheldon:)My god, those people need to learn
you can't just put "ye olde"...

20
00:01:01,414 --> 00:01:04,374
...in front of anything you want
and expect to get away with it.

21
00:01:04,543 --> 00:01:08,133
Can we please just go in?
My chain mail's stuck in my underwear.

22
00:01:09,631 --> 00:01:11,551
(Sheldon:)You're wearing modern underwear?

23
00:01:12,217 --> 00:01:14,297
(Leonard:)Relatively modern.

24
00:01:15,470 --> 00:01:16,550
(Leonard:)What are you wearing?

25
00:01:16,721 --> 00:01:20,681
(Sheldon:)I fashioned historically accurate
undergarments out of linen.

26
00:01:20,851 --> 00:01:22,181
You went and bought linen?

27
00:01:22,352 --> 00:01:25,562
(Sheldon:)Don't be silly.
I borrowed one of your pillowcases.

28
00:01:28,066 --> 00:01:30,066
(Leonard:)Borrowed?

